Okay, let me remember how to find midpoints. The midpoint formula is straightforward. If you have two points, say (x1,y1) and (x2,y2), the midpoint (Mx, My) is given by:

Mx = (x1 + x2) / 2

My = (y1 + y2) / 2

That seems right because you take the average of the x-coordinates and the average of the y-coordinates.

